From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:21:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: chrome: let an embedder open the tabs and windows
 extensions ask for

Plan C31. Extension APIs that need a browser window find none in an app that
embeds Chrome's browser process and shows its tabs itself
(chrome::EmbedderOwnsUI(), where Chrome's Browser windows are never
created): chrome.tabs.create failed with "No current window",
chrome.windows.create with "Browser windows not allowed", and
chrome.runtime.openOptionsPage resolved false.

Adds ExtensionTabUtil::SetEmbedderTabOpener() (EmbedderTabDisposition:
foreground tab, background tab, new window, popup). The embedder makes the
tab's WebContents in the given profile, starts loading the URL and hands it
to its UI; it returns that WebContents (no window, no index) or null. With
an opener set:

- tabs.create without a window id (or with the current window's) opens the
  tab through it (active or not); the extension gets the tab object.
  Extension pages of a spanning extension called from an incognito context
  open in the original profile, as Chrome falls back to a regular window;
  other off-the-record tabs, splitWithTabId and explicit window ids are
  errors.
- windows.create opens its first URL as a new window (a popup for type
  "popup"/"panel"), further URLs as background tabs, and returns a window
  object listing them. Moving an existing tab (tabId) and incognito windows
  are errors.
- runtime.openOptionsPage, and the "Extension options" link of
  chrome://extensions in an embedder tab, bring an embedder tab that already
  shows the options page forward (WebContentsDelegate::ActivateContents),
  as Chrome's singleton tab does, or open it in a new foreground tab
  (ExtensionTabUtil::OpenOptionsPageInEmbedder()).

Nothing changes when no embedder registers an opener.
---
